<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Viceroyalty of Kush</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 BCE – 1070 BCE (approx.) · capital Aniba</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Egypt's colonial administration of Nubia in the New Kingdom, governed by the 'King's Son of Kush' and rich in gold.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thutmose-i">Thutmose I</a> destroyed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kerma">Kerma</a> around 1500 BCE, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/egyptian-empire-new-kingdom">Egyptian Empire New Kingdom</a> annexed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a> as far as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile-cataracts">Fourth Cataract</a>. It was governed by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> with the title 'King's Son of Kush', divided into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wawat">Wawat</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-nubia">Lower Nubia</a>), administered from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aniba">Aniba</a>, and Kush (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-nubia">Upper Nubia</a>).</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroys</a> collected tribute in gold, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebony">ebony</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and soldiers, and Nubian gold mines in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadi-allaqi">Wadi Allaqi</a> made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> the richest power of its age. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">Pharaohs</a> built temple towns at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soleb">Soleb</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sesebi">Sesebi</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jebel-barkal">Gebel Barkal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-simbel">Abu Simbel</a>. Nubian elites were educated at the Egyptian court, and Egyptian religion, especially the cult of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amun">Amun</a>, took deep root. Known viceroys include <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merymose">Merymose</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amenhotep-huy">Huy</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 1080 BCE the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panehesy">Panehesy</a> fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/high-priest-of-amun">High Priest of Amun</a> in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a> and withdrew to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a>, which then slipped from Egyptian control. Egyptian religion and kingship persisted locally and later inspired the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kushite-empire">Kushite Empire of Napata</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="other, 1500 BCE – 1070 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">other</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:29.85%;width:8.56%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 BCE – 1070 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century-bce">16th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/11th-century-bce">11th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Aniba</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Merymose, Huy, Panehesy</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Egyptian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Egyptian, Nubian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/sudan">Sudan</a>, <a href="/countries/egypt">Egypt</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Egyptian Nubia, Kings Son of Kush</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1285&amp;focus=viceroyalty-